`add_clause` called `mk_literal(e)` twice for the same expression — once to check for `true_literal`/`false_literal`, then again unconditionally when storing into `lits[]`. The second call is pure waste: re-internalization, bool-var lookup, and rewrite checks with no new information.

## Change

```cpp
// Before
literal lit = mk_literal(e);
if (lit == true_literal) return;
if (lit != false_literal)
    lits[idx++] = mk_literal(e);  // redundant

// After
literal lit = mk_literal(e);
if (lit == true_literal) return;
if (lit != false_literal)
    lits[idx++] = lit;             // use already-computed value
```

