When `dns.getDefaultResultOrder()` returns `'verbatim'`, Node's `dns.lookup` already resolves in verbatim order — the two lookups can never differ, so there's no reason to schedule them.

## Changes

- **Early sync return**: Check `dns.getDefaultResultOrder() === 'verbatim'` synchronously at the top; return `undefined` immediately, skipping both DNS lookups and all async overhead
- **Remove `async`**: Function is no longer `async`; return type becomes `Promise<string | undefined> | undefined`. All call sites use `await`, which handles a plain `undefined` return transparently
- **Non-verbatim path**: Converted from `async/await` body to `Promise.all(...).then(...)` to maintain the same behaviour

```ts
export function getLocalhostAddressIfDiffersFromDNS(): Promise<
  string | undefined
> | undefined {
  if (dns.getDefaultResultOrder() === 'verbatim') {
    return undefined  // sync, no Promise created
  }
  return Promise.all([
    dns.lookup('localhost'),
    dns.lookup('localhost', { verbatim: true }),
  ]).then(([nodeResult, dnsResult]) => {
    const isSame =
      nodeResult.family === dnsResult.family &&
      nodeResult.address === dnsResult.address
    return isSame ? undefined : nodeResult.address
  })
}
```
